{"findings":[{"finding":"The brand wordmark \"Hive Works\" and the demo user's initials \"SC\" are hardcoded into the requirement, but they should come from configuration (sign-in and users are out of scope, so this identity is pure fixture data).","reqId":"REQ-10","rubric":8,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The list operation accepts a status filter, but nothing says what happens when the filter value is missing, malformed or unsupported; no error path or AC covers it.","reqId":"REQ-5","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Nothing covers the in-flight state while a status change is pending (e.g. disabling the action button), so a double-activation could send two transitions, such as Start work followed by an unintended second change.","reqId":"REQ-19","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-4.1 only checks that each of the four operations \"returns a response\", so nothing observable confirms the \"exactly four and no others\" constraint beyond the edit/delete cases.","reqId":"REQ-4","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-9.6 and AC-9.7 check that \"the request row retains its original status\", which is a database-level check rather than a public surface; unlike AC-9.4, they don't say to verify through a get-by-ID response.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Only the Title error message text is specified; the UI messages for missing area and missing priority are undefined, even though REQ-14 requires a field error under each failing field.","reqId":"REQ-14","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Cancel behaviour in the create dialog (whether entered values are discarded and the dialog closes without a request) has no requirement or AC.","reqId":"REQ-12","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Creation times are stored in UTC (REQ-6) but displayed as a date with no timezone, and the spec never says which timezone decides the calendar date, so the list and detail screens could disagree with test expectations near midnight.","reqId":"REQ-23","rubric":1,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-21.1 depends on subjective judgments (\"readable text\", \"neutral\", \"near-black\") and gives no concrete colour values, so there is no objective pass/fail check for the \"specified badge colors\".","reqId":"REQ-21","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-16.1's loading state is a manual check of a transient condition, and the spec defines no way to hold or simulate the pending list request so it can be observed reliably.","reqId":"REQ-16","rubric":3,"severity":"low"}]}